{Board No. 2 - This game, opened by G. A. Heginbottom (Oxford) against E. Young (Cambridge), was a Three Knights game. Since the opening moves were not correctly played, we give them in order to point out to the players their omissions:} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Bc5 {Not considered the best defence.} 4. Bb5 ({White should have continued with} 4. Nxe5 Nxe5 5. d4 Bd6 6. dxe5 {, etc.}) 4... a6 5. Bxc6 bxc6 (5... dxc6 {would have saved the pawn; for if} 6. Nxe5 {then} Bxf2+ 7. Kxf2 Qd4+ {, and ...Qxe5, etc.}) 6. Nxe5 {, etc. White lost a piece on the 16th move. Source: The Field, 1 April 1893, p495} 0-1

